                <pb facs="0286" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1291: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-17T13:00:00+08:00">September 17, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 17—10:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>820. Legation’s 765, August 29, 5 p.m. Following is translation of last paragraph
                    of note, dated September 15, from Ministry of Foreign Affairs: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“This Ministry has referred the above by telegraph to the Yunnan
                            Provincial Government for consideration and action. A reply has <pb
                                facs="0287" n="189" xml:id="pg189"/> now been received stating that
                            it has telegraphed the commanding generals on the fronts to make an
                            investigation and to promptly return the lighters as well as to instruct
                            the various units scrupulously to protect foreigners.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
